        "checkedAt": "2026-10-30",
        "scope": "lesson",
        "notes": "Pass 1 (author sourcing, CM-41 S2, 2026-10-30): the Korea Meteorological Administration pages 한국 기후특성 (weather.go.kr) and 4계절이 뚜렷한 우리나라 (kma.go.kr kids) opened; both say Korea's four seasons are clearly marked; korea.do gives the summer share of the year's rain as 54% and the rainy season starting in the second half of June, and the kids page names 장마 as the summer weather. The note says 'more than half' and 'early in summer', no more than the quotes. English paraphrase.\nPass 2 (culture and facts check, 2026-10-30): both KMA pages opened again; '사계절이 뚜렷하게', '여름철 강수량이 710.9mm로 연 강수량의 54%' and the rainy season from 6.19 (Jeju) to 6.25 (central region) on korea.do, and '4계절이 뚜렷' and '여름철 ... 장마' on the kids page, match each clause. No UNESCO claim; the institution is 기상청 (Korea Meteorological Administration) on the access date. Holds.\nPass 3 (language and learning design, 2026-10-30): the token 장마 (jangma, converter) with 가; es and ko keep the one {ko:} token and the es has no Hangul outside it. Reviser: the ko read 오는 ... 오고 ... 오는; it now reads 초여름에는 비가 오래 이어지는 장마가 시작되고, 한 해 비의 절반 이상이 여름에 내려요. No age word, emoji, speaking UI or percentage in any locale.\nPass 4 (third pass, 2026-10-30): the revised en, es and ko read against both sources and F-CURR-002 §5.1 and §7.7 again; each claim says no more than its quotes; no copy claims native-speaker or expert review. The independent MAR culture review of the PR re-reads the sources."
